//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  Wickless Retest
//
//  Marks candles that opened without hesitation — a bearish candle whose high
//  equals its open (no upper wick), a bullish candle whose low equals its open
//  (no lower wick) — draws the open as a level, and alerts when price returns to
//  it. Same markers as the xGhozt Wickless Candles indicator, plus the levels,
//  the retest logic and the trade plan.
//
//  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  READ THIS BEFORE TRADING IT. It did not pass a backtest.
//
//  Tested on 15-minute bars, 2010-2020, across four equity indices and four
//  FX/commodity markets, at 4bps round-trip cost, searching 1,500 parameter
//  combinations with a three-way train/validate/test split:
//
//      as described (trend filter, tight stop at the swing, 1:1)
//          -0.78R per trade, 32% win rate against a 50% break-even
//      best variant found, scored on held-out data
//          still negative: roughly -0.18R per trade
//
//  Two things break it, and they are worth understanding because they are not
//  opinions about the setup, they are arithmetic:
//
//  1. THE TIGHT STOP. You enter AT the level, and the level IS the recent
//     high or low, so "stop just beyond the swing" makes the stop about 0.10%
//     of price on a 15-minute chart. A 4bp round trip is then 39% of everything
//     you risk. Widening the stop to 2 ATR cut that to 12% and improved results
//     substantially — it still was not enough to turn the setup positive.
//
//  2. THE RETEST ITSELF. With zero costs the setup still lost (-0.13R, 43.5%
//     win at 1:1). Price continues through these levels more often than it
//     reverses from them, so the level is not acting as support or resistance
//     in the way the setup assumes.
//
//  An earlier version of this test looked strongly profitable. That was a bug:
//  it allowed one bar to both move away from the level and return to it, and
//  OHLC data cannot say which happened first inside the bar. Fixing that
//  assumption erased the entire edge. If you find a backtest of this pattern
//  showing a large edge, check whether it makes the same assumption.
//
//  WHAT THIS SCRIPT IS STILL GOOD FOR: marking the levels, watching how price
//  behaves at them on your own instrument, and alerting you to retests so you
//  can judge them yourself. A discretionary trader filtering these setups by
//  context is doing something this backtest cannot measure. It was also never
//  tested on AUD/CHF — that data was not available here.
//  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
indicator("Wickless Retest", shorttitle = "Wickless", overlay = true,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ─── Detection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_D = "Wickless detection"
wickTol = input.float(0.0, "Max wick, as a fraction of the candle's range",
     minval = 0.0, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.01, group = G_D,
     tooltip = "0 = the wick must be exactly absent. 0.02 allows a wick up to 2% " +
               "of the bar's range, which catches near-misses from feed rounding. " +
               "Results were insensitive to this.")
minBody = input.float(0.0, "Min body, as a fraction of range", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0,
     step = 0.05, group = G_D,
     tooltip = "Filters out wickless dojis. Also had little effect in testing.")

// ─── Trend ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_T = "Trend filter"
useTrend  = input.bool(true, "Only take setups with the trend", group = G_T,
     tooltip = "As described: sell setups below the EMA, buy setups above it. " +
               "In testing, turning this OFF scored slightly better.")
trendLen  = input.int(50, "Trend EMA length", minval = 1, group = G_T)

// ─── Level behaviour ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_L = "Levels"
expiryBars = input.int(10, "Bars a level stays live", minval = 1, group = G_L)
minMoveAtr = input.float(3.0, "Price must move this far away first (ATR)",
     minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = G_L,
     tooltip = "Stops the candle triggering its own level. This was the single " +
               "most important parameter: below 2 ATR results were clearly worse.")
oneLevel   = input.bool(true, "Keep only the newest level per direction", group = G_L)

// ─── Trade plan ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_R = "Trade plan"
atrLength  = input.int(14,  "ATR length",  minval = 1, group = G_R)
slLookback = input.int(5,   "Swing lookback for the stop", minval = 1, group = G_R)
slBuffer   = input.float(0.2, "Breathing room beyond the swing (ATR)",
     minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = G_R)
minStopAtr = input.float(2.0, "Minimum stop distance (ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.5,
     group = G_R,
     tooltip = "0 reproduces the setup as described. Leaving it at 0 makes the " +
               "stop so tight that spread costs swamp the trade — this was the " +
               "second-biggest factor in testing.")
rr         = input.float(1.0, "Reward : risk", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = G_R)

// ─── Display ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_V = "Display"
showArrows = input.bool(true,  "Wickless arrows",     group = G_V)
showLines  = input.bool(true,  "Level lines",         group = G_V)
showPlan   = input.bool(true,  "Entry / stop / target on retest", group = G_V)
bullCol    = input.color(#089981, "Bullish", group = G_V)
bearCol    = input.color(#f23645, "Bearish", group = G_V)

// ─── Detection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
rng  = high - low
body = math.abs(close - open)
okBody = rng > 0 and (minBody <= 0 or body / rng >= minBody)

bearish = close < open
bullish = close > open
upperWick = high - open        // for a bearish candle the open is the top
lowerWick = open - low         // for a bullish candle the open is the bottom

wicklessBear = bearish and okBody and rng > 0 and upperWick / rng <= wickTol
wicklessBull = bullish and okBody and rng > 0 and lowerWick / rng <= wickTol

trendEma = ta.ema(close, trendLen)
atrVal   = ta.atr(atrLength)
uptrend  = close > trendEma

// The setup as described: bearish wickless in a downtrend, bullish in an uptrend.
setupShort = wicklessBear and (not useTrend or not uptrend)
setupLong  = wicklessBull and (not useTrend or uptrend)

plotshape(showArrows and wicklessBear, "Wickless bearish", style = shape.triangledown,
     location = location.abovebar, color = bearCol, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showArrows and wicklessBull, "Wickless bullish", style = shape.triangleup,
     location = location.belowbar, color = bullCol, size = size.tiny)
plot(useTrend ? trendEma : na, "Trend EMA", color = color.new(color.orange, 50))

// ─── Level bookkeeping ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Parallel arrays: price, direction, bar created, armed flag, and the drawn line.
var array<float> lvPrice = array.new_float()
var array<int>   lvDir   = array.new_int()
var array<int>   lvBar   = array.new_int()
var array<bool>  lvArmed = array.new_bool()
var array<line>  lvLine  = array.new_line()

retestShort = false
retestLong  = false
retestPrice = 0.0

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // 1. Drop expired levels.
    i = array.size(lvPrice) - 1
    while i >= 0
        if bar_index - array.get(lvBar, i) > expiryBars
            ln = array.get(lvLine, i)
            if not na(ln)
                line.delete(ln)
            array.remove(lvPrice, i)
            array.remove(lvDir, i)
            array.remove(lvBar, i)
            array.remove(lvArmed, i)
            array.remove(lvLine, i)
        i -= 1

    // 2. Retest check, using levels armed by an EARLIER bar. Arming happens in
    //    step 3, so one bar can never both arm a level and trigger it — OHLC
    //    cannot tell us which came first inside the bar, and assuming the
    //    convenient order is what makes a backtest of this pattern look good.
    j = array.size(lvPrice) - 1
    while j >= 0
        p = array.get(lvPrice, j)
        d = array.get(lvDir, j)
        if array.get(lvArmed, j)
            if d == -1 and high >= p
                retestShort := true
                retestPrice := p
            else if d == 1 and low <= p
                retestLong := true
                retestPrice := p
        if (d == -1 and retestShort and array.get(lvPrice, j) == retestPrice) or
           (d == 1 and retestLong and array.get(lvPrice, j) == retestPrice)
            ln = array.get(lvLine, j)
            if not na(ln)
                line.set_extend(ln, extend.none)
                line.set_x2(ln, bar_index)
            array.remove(lvPrice, j)
            array.remove(lvDir, j)
            array.remove(lvBar, j)
            array.remove(lvArmed, j)
            array.remove(lvLine, j)
        j -= 1

    // 3. Arm levels that price has now travelled far enough away from.
    k = 0
    while k < array.size(lvPrice)
        if not array.get(lvArmed, k)
            p = array.get(lvPrice, k)
            d = array.get(lvDir, k)
            if d == -1 and low <= p - minMoveAtr * atrVal
                array.set(lvArmed, k, true)
            else if d == 1 and high >= p + minMoveAtr * atrVal
                array.set(lvArmed, k, true)
        k += 1

    // 4. Register this bar's setup.
    if setupShort or setupLong
        d = setupShort ? -1 : 1
        if oneLevel
            m = array.size(lvPrice) - 1
            while m >= 0
                if array.get(lvDir, m) == d
                    ln = array.get(lvLine, m)
                    if not na(ln)
                        line.delete(ln)
                    array.remove(lvPrice, m)
                    array.remove(lvDir, m)
                    array.remove(lvBar, m)
                    array.remove(lvArmed, m)
                    array.remove(lvLine, m)
                m -= 1
        array.push(lvPrice, open)
        array.push(lvDir, d)
        array.push(lvBar, bar_index)
        array.push(lvArmed, false)
        array.push(lvLine, showLines
             ? line.new(bar_index, open, bar_index + 1, open, extend = extend.right,
                        color = d == -1 ? bearCol : bullCol, width = 1)
             : na)

// ─── Trade plan on a retest ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
swingHigh = ta.highest(high, slLookback)[1]
swingLow  = ta.lowest(low, slLookback)[1]

planEntry = retestPrice
rawStopS  = math.max(nz(swingHigh, planEntry), planEntry) + slBuffer * atrVal
rawStopL  = math.min(nz(swingLow, planEntry), planEntry) - slBuffer * atrVal
riskS     = math.max(rawStopS - planEntry, minStopAtr * atrVal)
riskL     = math.max(planEntry - rawStopL, minStopAtr * atrVal)

planStop   = retestShort ? planEntry + riskS : planEntry - riskL
planTarget = retestShort ? planEntry - riskS * rr : planEntry + riskL * rr

if showPlan and (retestShort or retestLong)
    col = retestShort ? bearCol : bullCol
    label.new(bar_index, planEntry,
         (retestShort ? "SELL " : "BUY ") + str.tostring(planEntry, format.mintick) +
         "\nSL " + str.tostring(planStop, format.mintick) +
         "\nTP " + str.tostring(planTarget, format.mintick),
         style = retestShort ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
         color = col, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
    line.new(bar_index, planStop,   bar_index + 8, planStop,
         color = color.new(bearCol, 40), style = line.style_dashed)
    line.new(bar_index, planTarget, bar_index + 8, planTarget,
         color = color.new(bullCol, 40), style = line.style_dashed)

// ─── Alerts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(setupShort or setupLong, "Wickless setup formed",
     "Wickless: new level on {{ticker}} @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(retestShort, "Retest — sell setup",
     "Wickless: SELL retest on {{ticker}} @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(retestLong,  "Retest — buy setup",
     "Wickless: BUY retest on {{ticker}} @ {{close}}")

if retestShort
    alert("Wickless SELL retest " + syminfo.ticker + " @ " +
         str.tostring(planEntry, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if retestLong
    alert("Wickless BUY retest " + syminfo.ticker + " @ " +
         str.tostring(planEntry, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
